1. She is British. (Verbatim: "yeah um i'm british okay we're not very adventurous we're not adventurous")
2. She has a strong emotional reaction to sad stories, particularly about loyalty and loss. (Verbatim: "it's such a sad story like i i i know i can't think about it too hard because like i remember there was a futurama episode kind of based around it and and i wasn't ready for such feels")
3. She visited Hachiko's memorial in Shibuya and purchased multiple Hachiko-themed merchandise items. (Verbatim: "this is hachiko in shibuya and um if you if you um don't know of hachiko i recommend looking up the story it's really sad though um they have a lot of hachiko merch in shibuya by the way um like a lot of hachiko merch um that i might have bought a lot of")
4. She finds the 4D cinema experience stressful due to strict entry rules and the need to transfer items to a plastic bag. (Verbatim: "it was very odd um yeah it's very strange it i think it only works for action films um it was an experience it's not i would i want to try just watching this uh film normally i'll be honest")
5. She prefers safe, familiar food options and avoids adventurous or unusual flavors. (Verbatim: "i'm not brave i'm british okay we're not very adventurous we're not adventurous so if someone hands me any of these favorite popcorns i'm sorry i'm too scared and it's expensive popcorn costs money and i didn't want to waste it")
6. She enjoys chicken nuggets and considers them a comfort food, especially after emotional moments. (Verbatim: "my thought process was let's cheer myself up with some chicken nuggets")
7. She finds Japanese barbecue sauce and mustard sauce unfamiliar and cannot recall their exact names. (Verbatim: "they have mustard sauce which we don't have here and i actually can't remember what these two were i think one of them is one of them the teriyaki sauce or is that the barbecue i don't know")
8. She visited Shibuya Sky for panoramic views of Tokyo and purchased a drink there. (Verbatim: "here is um oh what was it called um i would say shibuya sky shibuya sky there's like a really tall building um you can go to and i went to it um yeah so this is the shibuya sky um thingy where that's where i got all my hachiko merch from um and i got this drink and the view is really cool")
9. She noticed that churros in Japan were served both warm and cold, which surprised her. (Verbatim: "these two churros were warm these two were were cold very strange this one was like um covered in like raspberry flakes and this one was just sugar flavored")
10. She has a preference for caramel and butter popcorn flavors, which are not commonly available in England. (Verbatim: "i definitely wanted to try caramel and they had butter as well so yeah no we don't do cheese popcorn here now no no i've never seen cheese popcorn here um and yeah caramel um you could probably buy it from the shop but yeah um") [end of text]



1. She has a fear of crowds and experiences agoraphobia. (Verbatim: "i have a literal fear of crowds going to like the most crowded places on the world")
2. She underwent therapy to help manage her agoraphobia and regain confidence in going outside. (Verbatim: "i actually had a lot of um therapy to help me go back outside and stuff um to help deal with my agoraphobia")
3. She visited Shibuya Sky in Tokyo and found the experience overwhelming due to heat despite being on a high floor. (Verbatim: "it was it was boiling i was boiling i was melting")
4. She enjoys churros, creme brulee, and macarons. (Verbatim: "i saw a lot of churros creme brulee and and macarons but yeah it was such an odd pack of half cold and half warm churros")
5. She visited Tokyo Disneyland and Tokyo DisneySea during her trip to Japan. (Verbatim: "we went to disney we went to disney um she took me to to disney")
6. She has a tendency to be easily scared by rides, even when others encourage her to try them. (Verbatim: "i was normally be very very very much too scared to go on um")
7. She was convinced by a friend to go on multiple rides she initially feared, only to discover her friend was also scared. (Verbatim: "she starts freaking out getting all scared and i'm like no wait wait wait wait you said this was safe")
8. She has a strong emotional reaction to being mistaken for someone else, especially when people try to flirt with her. (Verbatim: "who's flirting with me eh where and she was like right in front of you and i was like whoa oh no and then i ran away")
9. She has a close friendship with fellow YouTuber Lily Endo, who is graduating soon. (Verbatim: "lily ando's actually graduating this weekend i have no streams my plan is to watch")
10. She dreams of visiting Disneyland in addition to DisneySea, with plans to go with her friend Elp. (Verbatim: "so i do want to go to disneyland i think the plan is disneyland with elp which is me lily pandora") [end of text]



1. She has a strong emotional connection to Japan and considers her trip there a lifelong dream fulfilled. (Verbatim: "I already fulfilled my dream of living in Japan so I feel warm and fuzzy when I see other people get to experience it even more.")
2. She is British and resides in England. (Verbatim: "I'm British so I'm in England well it's not morning anymore it was morning when I started this stream.")
3. She enjoys sharing travel experiences and plans to create content compiling useful advice from her Japan trip. (Verbatim: "I want to collate all the advice that I found useful because I had to look in a lot of different places.")
4. She has a deep affection for animals and plans to do future streams focused on them. (Verbatim: "I really love animals they're just like they're just so cute they're just Pokémon.")
5. She plans to create a dedicated stream about her anime figurines with high-quality photography. (Verbatim: "I will give them a very good photo shoot and make sure I do a nice talk about them all.")
6. She is an introvert who identifies with being a "shut-in weeb" and finds socializing challenging. (Verbatim: "As an introvert I think my specific taste but then I also have all my Mount Fuji advices.")
7. She has a fear of horror games and considers herself a "scaredy-cat." (Verbatim: "I'm too scaredy-cat for this! Please, someone hold my hand!")
8. She enjoys eating sushi with soy sauce, which she considers a personal indulgence not typically done in Japan. (Verbatim: "I did as soon as I got back... I was like yo where my California chicken roll at where's my sushi?")
9. She values consistency in streaming but admits she currently lacks it, though she plans to improve after her debut. (Verbatim: "Currently my consistency is in the bin but I will be once I debut.")
10. She is planning to create short-form content using her new VTuber form. (Verbatim: "Maybe like my idea is to do little shorts or something once I have my new form.") [end of text]



1. She identifies as British. (Verbatim: "regular after your debut oh the fun part about being british is i'm allowed to butcher the english language and say it wrong because british people don't know how to speak it the most that is my british advices")
2. She enjoys the freedom to speak English in a non-standard way due to her British identity. (Verbatim: "i'm allowed to butcher the english language and say it wrong because british people don't know how to speak it")
3. She finds humor in the idea that authentic British people "murder" their language. (Verbatim: "um that's how you tell if someone's truly british they absolutely murder their language")
4. She has a habit of waking up early for streams, often appearing sleepy. (Verbatim: "honestly i love your morning streams we get to hear your sleepy voice")
5. She feels comfortable being sleepy during streams and considers it acceptable. (Verbatim: "sleepy is okay sleepy is okay sleepy is best")
6. She enjoys the cozy atmosphere of her morning streams, often using a blanket. (Verbatim: "i'm caught up on my chair all cozy cozy so yeah yeah yeah yeah yeah colin arigato arigato no thank you for being here i was nice no i should be thanking you honestly i'm able to be here because you're all here and supporting me so you know i'm eternally grateful")
7. She likes to nap on her sofa after streams. (Verbatim: "i am going to nap on my sofa")
8. She enjoys playing games like Baldur's Gate. (Verbatim: "i will be back tomorrow evening to play boulder's gate")
9. She has difficulty with game mechanics, such as understanding story progression in Baldur's Gate. (Verbatim: "i was kicking myself about that and i was like damn it i i i i've misinterpreted the game")
10. She enjoys music-based gameplay, as shown by her enthusiasm for gathering instruments and fighting with music. (Verbatim: "we fight to gather your flutes and violins the birds shall take flight and take flight to be fly") [end of text]



1. She has a strong affection for crème brûlée. (Verbatim: "i love creme brulee i love i love i love creme brulee")
2. She visited a crème brûlée-only food truck in Kyoto. (Verbatim: "when i was in kyoto there was a creme brulee van")
3. She finds it difficult to eat crème brûlée without making a mess. (Verbatim: "it was just so messy i tried though")
4. She has difficulty finding crème brûlée in England. (Verbatim: "whenever i go for food in england i'll go ask for the dessert menu look at it check for creme brulee no creme brulee")
5. She cried when crème brûlée was out of stock in England. (Verbatim: "then i'll cry um so i was so happy to see that they had creme brulee")
6. She visited Japan in July. (Verbatim: "so this is from july and it was baking hot")
7. She plans to return to Japan to experience cherry blossoms, autumn leaves in Hokkaido, and KFC Christmas. (Verbatim: "i want to see the cherry blossoms and i want to see the the autumn leaves in hokkaido and i want to experience a kfc christmas")
8. She found the heat in Japan more bearable than in England. (Verbatim: "i found that the heat in japan actually more bearable than um than super hot summer time in england")
